# Phaser Game Technology Stack

<version>1.0.0</version>

## Context
- Applied to all TypeScript files in the Circle Gladiator Army Arena (CGAA) game
- Ensures consistent implementation of game features using the established technology stack
- Maintains architectural consistency across the codebase

## Technology Stack Components
- **Core Framework**: Phaser 3 for game development
- **Language**: TypeScript for type safety and better maintainability
- **Build Tool**: Vite for fast development and optimized production builds
- **Testing Framework**: Vitest with JSDOM for component and unit testing
- **Physics Engine**: Phaser's Arcade Physics system with custom extensions
- **Module System**: ES Modules for code organization
- **Asset Handling**: Programmatically generated assets for performance optimization

## Requirements
- Use Phaser 3 Scene-based architecture for game state management
- Implement TypeScript interfaces and types for all game entities
- Organize code using component-based architecture
- Use object pooling for frequently created/destroyed game objects
- Implement proper event handling through Phaser's event system
- Apply Arcade Physics for collision detection and movement
- Write tests using Vitest for all game components
- Use procedural generation for textures and game elements when appropriate

## Examples

<example>
// Good: Proper scene structure with lifecycle methods
export class MainGame extends Scene {
  constructor() {
    super({ key: "MainGame" });
  }
  
  create() {
    // Setup game objects and event handlers
    this.createPlayer();
    this.createEnemies();
    this.setupEventListeners();
  }
  
  update(time: number, delta: number) {
    // Update game state
    this.player.update(delta);
    this.enemyManager.update(delta);
  }
}
</example>

<example>
// Good: Object pooling implementation
export class BulletPool {
  private pool: Bullet[] = [];
  private scene: Scene;
  
  constructor(scene: Scene, size: number) {
    this.scene = scene;
    // Pre-create all bullets
    for (let i = 0; i < size; i++) {
      const bullet = new Bullet(scene);
      bullet.setActive(false).setVisible(false);
      this.pool.push(bullet);
    }
  }
  
  get(): Bullet | null {
    return this.pool.find(bullet => !bullet.active) || null;
  }
}
</example>

